Subject: [PATCH 02079/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE C1
 (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING -- the mandated self-learning experiment) --
 re-power the online verifier-weight adaptation test on the LARGER family set.
 research-program.md mandates >=1 self-learning experiment/milestone; Tier 1 =
 online weight/counter updates (CPU, <1us/update, NOT the retired live-LoRA
 path). .395 found static-is-the-ceiling BUT the (online-static) CI only
 TOUCHED 0 at n=52 ([0.0, 0.192]) -- an n-limit, not a proven null. RE-RUN the
 Tier-1 online reweighting across the COMBINED family set (the .395 recovered
 manifest + ARC-GEN's many families from exp4282, a soft input) so the CI is
 POWERED, AND add a Tier-2 constraint-memory arm (cache per-family selection
 patterns, reuse on the nearest-neighbor seen family) as a distinct mechanism.
 Report static vs online vs Tier-2 cross-family delta + the per-family
 adaptation curve + a POWERED CI95 on (online-static). Emit
 online_adaptation_helps BARE bool := (online-static>0 AND CI95-excl-0). A
 positive gain = the verifier self-improves toward generalization
 (north-star-grade); a null WITH POWER = static is genuinely the ceiling
 (retire the online-adaptation-helps ask). verifier_is_oracle=false. NO
 fine-tuning; NO TRM; NO live-LoRA.

